{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Seven altars</b> — R. Abraham ibn Ezra hinted at a profound secret in this. Now Balaam wished to draw the divine favor upon himself through these offerings, and therefore he offered burnt offerings for all of them, and he wanted Balak himself to be occupied with them. Therefore Scripture says, \"And Balak and Balaam offered a bull and a ram on each altar\" — this one slaughters and that one dashes the blood. And the sense of \"And he said to him, The seven altars have I prepared\" (Numbers 23:4) is the way of prayer, as if to say: I have prepared before you a complete altar with a complete offering; may they find favor upon your altar's desire — in the manner that Scripture says: \"May He remember all your meal-offerings, and may your burnt-offering be made fat, selah\" (Psalms 20:4), and it says: \"Burnt-offerings of fatlings I will offer to you with the incense of rams; I will prepare cattle with goats, selah\" (Psalms 66:15), and so in many places. And the reason for the definite article, R. Abraham ibn Ezra already mentioned it. Now at the end, when Balaam did not wish to go toward the divinations, Balaam did not want Balak to be the one offering his offerings, lest he profane them in his intention, and therefore Scripture says: \"And he offered a bull and a ram on the altar\" (Numbers 23:30), hinting at Balaam who is the one mentioned. And it is possible that Balak offered them himself, for to appease his mind he did so, while Balaam no longer desired them:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The word נְחָשִׁים literally means 'serpents' but in context refers to divinations or omens; translated hyper-literally as 'divinations' to preserve Ramban's usage. The phrase מַעֲלֶה בְּקָרְבְּנוֹתָיו is rendered literally; the concern is that Balak's improper thought (מַחְשַׁבְתּוֹ) would invalidate the offerings — a technical sacrificial concept (פִּגּוּל)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:07.008554792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}